          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जीमणो (jīmaṇo) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from jemana, \"eating\". CDIAL lists Old Marwari jīmaṇa under it (CDIAL 5268). The Old Marwari row means \"food, meal\", and Old Gujarati jimaṇaüṃ means \"to the righthand side\": the right is the eating hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
